---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { production } from '../config/site';
import release from '../config/release.json';
---

<Base
  title="Cookies & Website Storage | EfiOps"
  description="Cookies and similar technologies used by the EfiOps website."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Website storage</p>
      <h1>Cookies and similar technologies.</h1>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="container legal">
    {!production && (
      <p class="preview-note">
        Review notice: the final host and any additional services must be checked before launch.
      </p>
    )}
    <section>
      <h2>The website as built</h2>
      <p>
        Fonts, the logo and illustrations are served with the website. Advertising pixels, booking
        widgets and external media embeds are disabled.
        {production && release.analyticsEnabled
          ? 'Google Analytics is optional. Its script is loaded only after you choose Accept analytics. Rejecting it does not affect your ability to use the website.'
          : 'Google Analytics is not loaded in this review build.'}
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Analytics choices and cookies</h2>
      <p>
        Your accept/reject choice is remembered in your browser’s local storage for up to 180 days.
        You can change it through Cookie settings in the footer. If you accept, Google Analytics may
        set first-party cookies such as _ga and _ga_P6T446WBEN, typically lasting up to two years
        depending on the stream settings. We use analytics to understand page use and count accepted
        website enquiries. We do not send form names, email addresses or message text as analytics
        event parameters. Advertising consent remains denied.
      </p>
      <p>
        Rejecting analytics prevents its script from loading. Withdrawing consent removes accessible
        Analytics cookies and reloads the page to stop the running script. It does not delete
        information already received by Google; contact karol@efiops.com about information requests.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Your enquiry</h2>
      <p>
        The form uses a random request identifier to help prevent duplicate submissions. It is held
        in the page while it is open, rather than stored in a cookie or local storage. After an
        accepted enquiry, a temporary acceptance timestamp in session storage allows the
        confirmation page to show the received message. That timestamp contains no enquiry details
        and is removed when the confirmation page loads.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Dashboard sign-in</h2>
      <p>
        The admin dashboard uses essential authentication cookies to keep its authorised owner
        signed in. These cookies are HttpOnly, are restricted to dashboard API requests and use
        Secure protection on HTTPS. They are cleared on sign-out. This storage is used for access
        security, not advertising or analytics.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>If optional services change</h2>
      <p>
        Before enabling optional tracking or embedded services, EfiOps must review their storage,
        purposes and provider arrangements, update this notice and provide appropriate controls.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Questions about information</h2>
      <p>
        <a href="/privacy/">Read how EfiOps handles your information.</a>
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
